    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "http://grounding-service:8000/falcon/map",
        "options": {},
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ alerts: $('falcon_hydrate').item.json.resources }) }}"
      },
      "id": "falcon_map",
      "name": "falcon_map",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.4,
      "position": [
        1440,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "// Post each Falcon-mapped alert to the existing honeypot-triage webhook, oldest-first,\n// collecting ack results. Stops at the first failure so a partial failure never double-triages a\n// later alert; grounding-service advance_state then honors only the contiguous-ok prefix (no SKIP).\n// .first() (not .item): \"Run Once for All Items\" has no current item for .item to pair to.\nconst items = $('falcon_map').first().json.items || [];\nconst results = [];\nfor (const it of items) {\n  let ok = false;\n  try {\n    await this.helpers.httpRequest({\n      method: 'POST',\n      url: 'http://10.0.0.6:5678/webhook/honeypot-triage',\n      body: it.body,\n      json: true,\n    });\n    ok = true;\n  } catch (e) {\n    ok = false;\n  }\n  results.push({ composite_id: it.composite_id, created: it.created, ok });\n  if (!ok) break;                       // contiguous prefix only — un-acked tail retries next tick\n}\nreturn [{ json: { results } }];"
      },
      "id": "post-collect",
      "name": "Post+Collect",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1664,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "http://grounding-service:8000/falcon/advance",
        "options": {},
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ results: $('Post+Collect').item.json.results }) }}"
      },
      "id": "falcon_advance",
      "name": "falcon_advance",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.4,
      "position": [
        2048,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 📡 falcon-alert-poller\n**What it does:** Every 15 minutes it pulls any new CrowdStrike Falcon alerts and feeds them into the shared `honeypot-triage` webhook.\n\n**Why:** Falcon can't push to a webhook, so we poll it instead. This workflow is purely a feeder, and once an alert is forwarded it flows through the same downstream triage pipeline as the Splunk path.",
        "height": 168,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky-doc---how-it-works",
      "name": "Doc — How It Works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -64,
        -400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ⚙️ Setup / prerequisites\n- **CrowdStrike OAuth2** credential (`Crowdstrike Falcon Account`), cloud **us-2**.\n- **grounding-service** at `http://grounding-service:8000` for `/falcon/state|plan|map|advance`.\n- Posts to `http://10.0.0.6:5678/webhook/honeypot-triage`.",
        "height": 168,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "sticky-doc---setup",
      "name": "Doc — Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        432,
        -400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 📌 Notes\n- It's **stateful** (it tracks a `watermark` and a bounded `seen` list), so it triages each alert once and survives restarts.\n- The FQL filter is `created_timestamp` on its own, because n8n can't transmit the FQL `+` AND.\n- On an empty state the watermark defaults to `now-24h` (fix #10), so a fresh start can't get stuck in a 400-loop.\n- Activate the Schedule Trigger to run it unattended.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "sticky-doc---notes",
      "name": "Doc — Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        192,
        -624
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ① Poll & Plan\n**What it does:** On a 15-minute timer it reads the `{watermark, seen}` state, asks Falcon for any alerts created since the watermark (oldest-first), then drops already-seen IDs and caps how many it processes per run.\n\n**Why:** so it only ever processes genuinely new alerts. The `IF has_new` node ends the run cleanly when there's nothing to do.",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 1128,
        "color": "#030303"
      },
      "id": "sticky-section---poll-&-plan",
      "name": "Section — Poll & Plan",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -64,
        -208
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ② Hydrate, Map & Forward\n**What it does:** It fetches the full alert objects, reshapes each one into the common Splunk-style body (sorted oldest-first), and POSTs each to the `honeypot-triage` webhook, collecting an ack for each one until the first failure.\n\n**Why:** both feeders use the same body shape, so everything flows into one downstream pipeline. It stops at the first failed POST so a later alert can't slip through ahead of an earlier one.",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 720,
        "color": "#000000"
      },
      "id": "sticky-section---hydrate,-map-&-forward",
      "name": "Section — Hydrate, Map & Forward",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1120,
        -208
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ③ Advance State\n**What it does:** It moves the `watermark` and `seen` list forward across the *contiguous* run of successful POSTs, and no further.\n\n**Why:** that way a mid-batch failure never strands an earlier alert behind the watermark. Anything that wasn't acked just gets retried on the next tick, so nothing is skipped.",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 420,
        "color": "#030303"
      },
      "id": "sticky-section---advance-state",
      "name": "Section — Advance State",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1888,
        -208
      ]
    }
  ],
